theory.intro:
Volume is the amount of space a solid takes up. For a rectangular prism (box), multiply the three dimensions together.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3,1.5);
\coordinate (D) at (0,1.5);
\coordinate (E) at (1.386,0.8);
\coordinate (F) at (4.386,0.8);
\coordinate (G) at (4.386,2.3);
\coordinate (H) at (1.386,2.3);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,below,font=\small] {length};
\draw (D)--(A) node[midway,left,font=\small] {height};
\draw (B)--(F) node[midway,below right,font=\small] {width};
\draw (B)--(C)--(D);
\draw (F)--(G)--(C);
\draw (D)--(H)--(G);
\draw[dashed] (A)--(E)--(F);
\draw[dashed] (E)--(H);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

